#!/usr/bin/env python3
# Phase 435 in CLAUDE.md: the Phase row (a plan; nothing applied).   python3 claudemd435.py <CLAUDE.md>
import sys
p = sys.argv[1]; s = open(p, encoding='utf-8').read()
if '| 435 | 2026-10-12 |' in s: raise SystemExit('CLAUDE.md: row 435 already there')
row = """| 435 | 2026-10-12 | **Plan: the path in levels (not applied).** Her 11:17: real lessons zigzag (a little rhythm, a little note reading) -- should the course go stage by stage, all of pitch before rhythm? Her 11:19 '좋아. 그렇게 해보자' to: the townhouse floors become LEVELS; every floor mixes playing, pitch, rhythm and music rooms; free order inside a floor with a suggested zigzag (running numbers 1-27); 'after' rooms noted, never locked; each room's book teaches its floor's part, harder parts stay in its drill's higher levels (with their grade) or move to the room that fits. Plan v1 (Claude outputs/Course-levels-plan-v1.pdf; _workspace/chapter-review/g435/x/plan: levels.json, rooms.json, the house mock drawn by townhouseSvg with 5 floors): Floor 1 First lessons (Posture, Keyboard patterns, Pulse, Musical alphabet, Notes & rests, Reading the staff); 2 Reading and counting (Whole staff, Time signatures, Steps & skips, Loud & soft, Tones & semitones, Pitch & range); 3 Going further (Tempo, Rhythm patterns, Ledger lines, Scales, Accidentals -- a NEW room: the natural, a sign lasts until the bar line --, The piano's story); 4 Keys and chords (Key signatures, Signs, Intervals, Chords, Composers, Melody); 5 Shaping music (Form, Terms, Styles). AMEB per room (Preliminary complete at the end of floor 4); no grade names on floors. A fresh reviewer checked order, prerequisites, floors and AMEB; its fixes are in (the quaver pair into Notes & rests; Tones after Whole staff; Pulse and Notes & rests cut back, strong/weak beats, bars, rests on the staff, the repeat sign and the tie to Time signatures; bar lines taught once; AMEB column corrected; Know-the-music rooms spread; the house line 'Start · floor by floor, any room first'). Decisions C1-C10 wait for her (floors and rooms, names, spread, numbers, never locked, room scope, the six finished books renumbered with references by name, short room names, next books in path order, an AMEB checklist later). |
"""
i = s.index('| 434 | 2026-10-12 |'); j = s.index('\n', i) + 1
s = s[:j] + row + s[j:]
open(p, 'w', encoding='utf-8').write(s); print('CLAUDE.md ok')
